    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nPotentially following from #714, mini.pick will not open URI paths generated by jdtls for decompiled class files from lsp actions. I am not sure whether this is specific to jdtls or more general.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0-dev-2826+gf6dcc464f\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Ensure mini.pick, mini.extra and the jdtls language server are installed and configured.\r\n2. Create a new Java project.\r\n3. In `App.java`, write\r\n```java\r\npackage org.example;  // relevant package name\r\n\r\npublic class App {\r\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\r\n        System.out.println(\"-\");\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n4. Move the cursor to `System` and call `require(\"mini.extra\").pickers.lsp({ scope = \"definition\" })`.\r\n5. Select the first and only option in the picker.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe URI should be opened in Neovim.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe URI is not opened, and `}` is printed below the statusline.",
