            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI don't have Java stack installed (and don't plan to at the moment), so would you mind helping me debug this? As `MiniExtra.pickers.lsp()` uses corresponding `vim.lsp.buf` methods, could execute the following command in the same conditions as when you'd call `lsp` picker:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-- Execute `vim.lsp.buf.definition()` but save the result instead of acting on it\r\n:lua vim.lsp.buf.definition({ on_list = function(...) _G.args = { ... } end })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen follow up with `:lua vim.fn.append(0, vim.split(vim.inspect(args), '\\n'))` which will paste `args` as text at the top of current buffer. Copy those lines and paste them here.",
