        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Then sorry, but this doesn't look like a 'mini.extra' issue. The argument to the `on_list` function is assumed to have `items` which is structured same as quickfix list (as per `:h vim.lsp.LocationOpts.OnList`). In quickfix list items can have `filename` field which is a \"name of a file\" (meaning full path, really). This is not the case in this example.\r\n\r\nI am not sure where the issue here is: either in `jdtls` itself or Neovim's handling of `on_list`.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"this doesn't look like a 'mini.extra' issue, sorry\".",
